  "verdict": "matches",
  "differences": [
    {
      "what": "Left of the hotel, the north side of Lake Street: the drawing's ten fronts from the far end to the hotel (a two-storey store, two stores, the three-storey hipped block, four two-storey stores, a store-dwelling and a one-storey shop) stand in the render in the drawn order, storeys, roof forms and false fronts, shoulder to shoulder up to the hotel's Lake gable. Before T-3605 this face held two cottages and open ground.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "what": "Right of the hotel, the west side of Dearborn: the seven gable-fronted stores and store-dwellings run north from the hotel to the alley as drawn. Before T-3605 the hotel's stable and Bates's auction room stood on this frontage; both now stand behind or after the row.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "what": "The two tall blocks at the far left, across Clark Street, stand as three-storey blocks at the drawn place.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "what": "Widths of the far Lake stores: the drawing compresses the far end of the row, so the far stores take frontages in proportion to their bays between Clark Street and the hotel rather than the camera's 14-16 m; their order, storeys and roofs are as drawn, and the difference is in how far apart two readings of one drawn row put each party line.",
      "status": "within tolerance"
